---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Button from "../components/Button.astro";
import {publicProducts} from "../data/products";
---
<Base title="Support" description="Find setup help and approved release resources for BORGAS racing and diagnostic products."><section class="section"><div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">Owner support</p><h1>Start with your product.</h1><p class="lede">Have the product code, hardware revision and software version ready. They help us match the guidance to your device.</p><nav class="filters" aria-label="Choose a support product">{publicProducts().map(p=><a href={"#"+p.slug}>{p.code}</a>)}</nav>{publicProducts().map(p=><article class="support-row" id={p.slug}><div><p class="eyebrow">{p.code}</p><h2>{p.name}</h2><p>{p.id==="brc-02"?"If the dashboard stays on standby, check that USB is connected to the native ESP32-S3 port and that SimHub is sending telemetry. The waiting caption distinguishes a missing connection from missing valid telemetry.":p.id==="brc-fl"?"The flag panel uses its own SimHub serial-device configuration. Its formula must match the dashboard's telemetry format.":"Match the device identity and hardware revision before installing firmware or following setup instructions."}</p></div><div><h3>Help & resources</h3>{p.resources.length?p.resources.map(r=><p><a href={r.href}>{r.title} ↗</a><br/><span class="small">{r.note} Release index and files hosted on GitHub; select the matching model and version there.</span></p>):<p>Contact BORGAS for the setup guide and files appropriate to your build.</p>}<div class="actions"><Button href={"/contact?product="+p.code+"&topic=Technical%20support"}>Ask about {p.code}</Button><a href={"/products/"+p.slug}>Product details</a></div></div></article>)}</div></section></Base>
